SUMMARY:Obituary: Sharon Stratton
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260804
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260805
DTSTAMP:20260808T131601Z
UID:wrightfuneralhomeobit-2026-08-04-sharon-stratton-2026-08-04-allday@lin
 n-county-scraper.local
CATEGORIES:obituary
DESCRIPTION:Sharon (Collier) Stratton\, age 84\, of Brookfield\, passed aw
 ay peacefully on Tuesday\, August 4\, 2026\, at Stonebridge Senior Living 
 in Chillicothe. A Celebration of Sharon’s Life will be held at a later d
 ate. Memorials to Laclede United Methodist Church may be left at or mailed
  to Wright Funeral Home\, P.O. Box 496\, Brookfield\, MO 64628. Sharon was
  born\, July 10\, 1942\, at her grandmother’s house in Brookfield.  She 
 was the first child to Paul and Grace Collier and always enjoyed being fir
 st.  She lived in Brookfield then moved to Laclede where her father worked
  with Burlington Northern Railroad and her mother worked at Henderson’s 
 then later at the Laclede Post Office.  Everyone around Laclede knew their
  family\, and soon\, in 1945\, her sister\, Karen\, came along.  A little 
 sister to play and have fun with!  Then in 1952\, baby brother\, Clifford 
 Ray\, had two big sisters to deal with.  Growing up was grand! Some troubl
 es came in 1953\, when Polio reared its ugly head and the girls had so man
 y trips to the hospital.  Laclede supported the whole family when they wer
 e struggling\, there was so much love as well. Sharon came out of it okay 
 but was always in the hospital looking out for little sister in those earl
 y days.  Once they were back in school\, there was baseball\, basketball\,
  4-H\, campfire girls\, and so many grandparents\, cousins\, neighbors\, f
 riends and classmates to come home too.  By senior year\, Sharon was at Me
 adville High School and graduated in 1960. By 1962\, she was a married lad
 y with a handsome husband named John Stratton\, that she met during her se
 nior year in Meadville.  She was then on to college where she graduated in
  1964 with a  bachelor’s degree in accounting and business management fr
 om Warrensburg.  She and John later moved to Chillicothe and Sharon starte
 d her career at City Bank\, as an accountant\, while John worked with fami
 ly running a tractor all over the county. Within the next few years Sharon
  became a Marine Corps wife and moved around a lot.  She lived in so many 
 places\, like Independence MO\, Kansas City MO\, Jacksonville NC\, and Nor
 folk VA\, and always found jobs working with numbers.  In Virginia\, she l
 oved to watch the ships in the bay come and go from her office window.  Jo
 hn was busy learning how to be a Marine and eventually serving in Vietnam.
   Life in the Marine Corps eventually brought them to California where Sha
 ron could be close to her beloved cousin\, Jean and all of her family.  Th
 en babies finally came along\, Craig in 1969 and Dona in 1972.  After a fe
 w more years\, jobs and lots of growing\, Sharon settled with her family i
 n Northern California. She became a business owner in Napa and helped seve
 ral generations of families and businesses with all their income tax\, boo
 kkeeping\, and investment needs.  She had a solid family\, a thriving busi
 ness\, and all she needed was a little more to keep her busy\, so she coac
 hed kids ball teams\, taught every child she knew to swim\, and still had 
 time to lead campfire girls and boy scout groups. Sharon and John also enj
 oyed raising dogs and puppies and collecting classic cars.  Then she remem
 bered how much she loved bowling!  She was an amazing bowler\, sponsored t
 eams\, made it into the local hall of fame\, enjoyed many city tournaments
 \, and also ran a local tournament for several years to benefit veterans. 
 Being far away from her Missouri home meant lots of trips to visit.  She a
 lways liked a houseful\, so many people came to live at the dream home she
  loved in Napa.  It got crowded at times\, but that’s how a California f
 amily was built\, and she enjoyed every minute of it! We lost our dear sis
 ter\, daughter\, wife\, mother\, aunt\, cousin and friend to Dementia.  It
  was a long hard battle\, but the care needed brought her back home to Mis
 souri\, where she was cared for by family\, new friends\, old friends\, an
 d a very special family that we found in Napa and somehow ended up with us
  right here in Missouri!  You know who you are\, and we love you. Sharon i
 s survived by numerous loving family members and friends who will cherish 
 her memory. She was preceded in death by beloved family whom she will joyf
 ully reunite with in Heaven. Sharon left this world on Tuesday\, August 4\
 , 2026\, at 8:00 p.m.\, at the age of 84.  She was surrounded by loved one
 s and the gentle hands of staff at Stonebridge Senior Living in Chillicoth
 e\, Three River’s Hospice\, and our home care team.  We are so grateful 
 for their care and for helping her achieve the peace that she was needing.
  Her family would like to thank everyone in Laclede\, Brookfield\, Meadvil
 le and Chillicothe for welcoming her home\, and to the countless caregiver
 s along the way that truly shared their whole hearts.\n\nFull obituary and
  service details: https://www.wright-funeralhome.com/obituaries/Sharon-Str
 atton?obId=49204979
LOCATION:Brookfield\, MO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Obituary: Conner  Lee  Spainhour
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260804
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260805
DTSTAMP:20260808T131601Z
UID:wrightfuneralhomeobit-2026-08-04-conner-lee-spainhour-2026-08-04-allda
 y@linn-county-scraper.local
CATEGORIES:obituary
DESCRIPTION:Conner Lee Spainhour\, age 22\, of Purdin\, Missouri\, passed 
 away Tuesday\, August 4\, 2026. Conner Lee\, son of Nickolas Spainhour and
  Tessa (Sackrey) Coffman\, was born March 15\, 2004\, in Chillicothe\, Mis
 souri. Conner was a 2022 graduate of Linn County R-1 High School near Purd
 in and a 2024 graduate of Linn State Technical College of Missouri.  He wa
 s currently employed at Scobee Powerline Construction as a lineman.  Conne
 r brought endless light\, laughter\, and kindness to everyone he met.  He 
 loved music\, duck hunting\, fishing\, and fireworks\, but more than anyth
 ing\, Conner treasured time spent with close friends and family.  Although
  Conner’s life ended far too soon\, his love and memories will continue 
 to live on through his family and friends.  He will be deeply missed and f
 orever remembered. Survivors include his mother and stepfather\, Tessa and
  Jeremy Coffman of Purdin\; his stepmother\, Courtney Spainhour of Chillic
 othe\; two brothers\, Alex Coffman of Purdin and Carlynn Spainhour of Chil
 licothe\; two sisters\, Tymber Spainhour of Chillicothe and Tenzli Brannam
  of Chillicothe\; his grandparents\, Doug and Monica Denton\, Ronnie and R
 achel Bowes\, and Rick and Janice Coffman\; and numerous aunts\, uncles\, 
 and cousins.  In addition to his family\, his is survived by his best frie
 nds: Brad James Sackrey\, Jr.\, Sam Becker\, Mason Singleton\, Gage Seals\
 , Case Ratliff\, and Jordan Bealmer. He was preceded in death by his fathe
 r\, Nickolas Spainhour\; and two grandfathers\, James Sackrey and Carlton 
 Spainhour. The family will receive friends Monday\, August 10\, 2026\, fro
 m 9:00 a.m. until 12:00 noon at Wright Funeral Home in Brookfield. A celeb
 ration of life\, for family and close friends\, will follow at 12:00 noon 
 with Pastor Sung Bauta officiating at the funeral home. The family kindly 
 requests that those attending the visitation dress in casual attire. Memor
 ial contributions to the family payable to Tessa Coffman may be left at or
  mailed to Wright Funeral Home P.O. 496\, Brookfield\, Missouri 64628.\n\n
 Full obituary and service details: https://www.wright-funeralhome.com/obit
 uaries/Conner-Lee-Spainhour?obId=49198194
LOCATION:Purdin\, MO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Obituary: Bobby Dale Hudson "Bob"
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260721
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260722
DTSTAMP:20260808T131601Z
UID:wrightfuneralhomeobit-2026-07-21-bobby-dale-hudson-bob-2026-07-21-alld
 ay@linn-county-scraper.local
CATEGORIES:obituary
DESCRIPTION:Bobby Dale Hudson was born on September 25\, 1952\, in Jamespo
 rt\, Missouri\, to Randall and Mary (Brown) Hudson. Bob passed away peacef
 ully at his home in Laclede\, MO\, with his family by his side after compl
 ications of diabetes. On November 4\, 1973\, Bob married his high school s
 weetheart\, Sandy Linebaugh. Together they built a marriage of more than 5
 2 years\, raising their family and sharing a lifetime of memories through 
 life's joys and challenges. Bob was a man who lived life on his own terms.
  Known for his stubborn determination\, strong opinions\, and having no fi
 lter\, he was someone who never pretended to be anything other than himsel
 f. Before losing his leg in 2012\, Bob had a lifelong love of horses and e
 njoyed spending countless hours riding. After his amputation\, he refused 
 to let that define him. Instead\, he found new ways to enjoy the outdoors\
 , whether driving the gravel roads in his beloved red Ford truck\, riding 
 his four-wheeler\, or putting around town in his golf cart. Although Bob c
 ould be gruff and was never known for sugarcoating his thoughts\, those cl
 osest to him knew the deep love he had for his family. He was proud of his
  children\, Rusty and Lindsey\, and bragged on them to others whenever he 
 had the chance. As the family grew\, Bob happily welcomed each new member.
  He embraced Jerry and Cassie\, and his bonus grandchildren\, Jacob\, Luke
 \, Seth\, and Cody\, loving them as members of his family. Nothing\, howev
 er\, compared to the love he had for his granddaughter\, Hazel. She quickl
 y became the center of his world\, bringing out a patience and gentleness 
 that surprised everyone who knew him. She held a special place in his hear
 t. On July 8\, 2026\, Bob accepted Jesus Christ as his Savior during a vis
 it with Brother Monty. In the days that followed\, he found a sense of pea
 ce and comfort and was thankful to spend his final days at home\, with his
  family nearby. Bob is survived by his wife\, Sandy Hudson\, of the home\;
  his son\, Rusty (Cassie) of Galt\; his daughter\, Lindsey (Jerry) Calvert
  of Rothville\; his Sister\, Marilyn Moulin of Gilman City\, MO\; his cher
 ished granddaughter\, Hazel Calvert\; his bonus grandchildren\, Jacob (Sab
 rina) Calvert of Liberty\, MO\; Luke (Abbi) Calvert of Biloxi\, MS\; Seth 
 (Jordan) Calvert of Sumter\, SC\; and Cody Blackwell of Richmond\, MO. Alo
 ng with many nieces and nephews. He was preceded in death by his parents\,
  Randall and Mary Hudson\; his brothers\, Bill and Randy Hudson\; and a st
 illborn son\, John Travis\, in 1976. Though he will be deeply missed\, his
  family finds comfort in knowing he is now free from pain and at peace wit
 h his Lord. A celebration of Bob’s life will be held at a later date. Me
 morial contributions toward Bob’s granddaughter\, Hazel’s college fund
  (payable to Lindsey Calvert) may be left at or mailed to Wright Funeral H
 ome\, P.O. Box 496\, Brookfield\, MO 64628.\n\nFull obituary and service d
 etails: https://www.wright-funeralhome.com/obituaries/Bobby-Dale-Hudson-Bo
 b?obId=49059013
LOCATION:Laclede\, MO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Obituary: Carol Gail Lee
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260807
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260808
DTSTAMP:20260808T131601Z
UID:delaneyfuneralhomeobit-2026-08-07-carol-gail-lee-2026-08-07-allday@lin
 n-county-scraper.local
CATEGORIES:obituary
DESCRIPTION:Carol Gail Lee\, 83\, of Marceline\, Missouri\, passed away pe
 acefully on Friday August 7\, 2026. Carol was born on May 6\, 1943\, in Br
 ashear\, Missouri\, to Rev. G.D. Hammontree and Bonnie Lee (Sullins) Hammo
 ntree. She spent her life devoted to her family and her Christian faith. O
 n June 9\, 1963\, Carol married the love of her life\, John Steven Lee. To
 gether they shared 65 years of marriage. Carol attended college and worked
  as a bookkeeper throughout her career. She was a faithful member of First
  Baptist Church\, where her faith served as a guiding light throughout her
  life. She is survived by her beloved husband\, John Steven Lee\; her son\
 , Nicholas Venneman (Shelby Stafford) of Chillicothe\, Missouri\; her daug
 hter\, Chelsey Venneman (Malachi Philips-Bey) of Marceline\, Missouri\; he
 r cherished grandchildren\, Jace Wills and Oaklee Venneman\; and her siste
 r\, Joann Foster\; and her twin brother\, G. Dale Hammontree. Carol was pr
 eceded in death by her daughter\, Kristi Renee Lee\; her parents\, Rev. G.
 D. Hammontree and Bonnie Lee Hammontree\; her sisters\, Peggy Payne and He
 len Minor\; her brothers-in-law\, D. L. Payne\, Frank Foster\, and Robert 
 E. Lee\; and her parents-in-law\, Eugene Lee and Mary Ethlyne Lee. A visit
 ation will be held on Tuesday\, August 11\, 2026\, beginning at 2:00 p.m.\
 , followed by a memorial service at 3:00 p.m. at the First Baptist Church 
 in Marceline\, Missouri. Psalm 23 The LORD Is My Shepherd A Psalm of David
 . [1] The LORD is my shepherd\; I shall not want. [2]  He makes me lie dow
 n in green pastures. He leads me beside still waters. [3]  He restores my 
 soul. He leads me in paths of righteousness for his name’s sake. [4] Eve
 n though I walk through the valley of the shadow of death\, I will fear no
  evil\, for you are with me\; your rod and your staff\, they comfort me. [
 5] You prepare a table before me in the presence of my enemies\; you anoin
 t my head with oil\; my cup overflows. [6] Surely goodness and mercy shall
  follow me all the days of my life\, and I shall dwell in the house of the
  LORD forever. (ESV)\n\nFull obituary and service details: https://www.del
 aneyfuneralhome.com/obituaries/Carol-Gail-Lee?obId=49204775
LOCATION:Marceline\, MO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Obituary: Kenneth Charles "Kenny" Gladbach
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260726
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260727
DTSTAMP:20260808T131601Z
UID:delaneyfuneralhomeobit-2026-07-26-kenneth-charles-kenny-gladbach-2026-
 07-26-allday@linn-county-scraper.local
CATEGORIES:obituary
DESCRIPTION:Kenneth Charles "Kenny" Gladbach\, age 61\, of Marceline\, Mis
 souri\, formerly of Mendon\, passed away at his home on Sunday\, July 26\,
  2026. Born on October 17\, 1964\, in Marceline\, Missouri\, Kenny was the
  son of Charles William Gladbach and Sharol Jo Martin. He proudly served h
 is country in the United States Marine Corps. On July 3\, 2000\, Kenny mar
 ried the love of his life\, Ethelyn Sue Davidson. Kenny dedicated more tha
 n 20 years of his career to Walsworth. Outside of work\, he enjoyed huntin
 g\, mowing the lawn\, attending tractor pulls\, and had an appreciation fo
 r anything John Deere. More than anything\, Kenny enjoyed spending time wi
 th his family. He was member of St. Joseph Catholic Church in Hurricane Br
 anch. Kenny is lovingly survived by his wife\, Sue Gladbach of the home\; 
 his children\, Blake Gladbach (Casie) of Maryville\, Nikki Gladbach of Mar
 celine\, Charles Tapscott (Breanna) of Columbia\, and Ashley Yount (Anthon
 y) of New Cambria\; 14 cherished grandchildren\; one great-grandchild\; hi
 s sister\, Sharol "Dee" White of Marceline\; his brother\, Kendall Gladbac
 h (Tamra) of Carrollton\; as well as several nieces\, nephews\, extended f
 amily members\, and many friends. He was preceded in death by his parents\
 ; his sister\, Deborah Reams\; and his maternal and paternal grandparents.
  Memorial donations to the family payable to Delaney Funeral Home may be l
 eft at or mailed to Delaney Funeral Home\, 1720 North Missouri Ave. Marcel
 ine\, MO 64658. A celebration of life will be held Saturday\, August 8\, 2
 026\, at Gods Garden Church in Brookfield at 1:00 p.m.. The family will re
 ceive friends from noon until the time of the service at the church.\n\nFu
 ll obituary and service details: https://www.delaneyfuneralhome.com/obitua
 ries/Kenneth-Charles-Gladbach?obId=49138904
LOCATION:Marceline\, MO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Obituary: Larrell Keith "Sam" Newlin
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260719
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260720
DTSTAMP:20260808T131601Z
UID:delaneyfuneralhomeobit-2026-07-19-larrell-keith-sam-newlin-2026-07-19-
 allday@linn-county-scraper.local
CATEGORIES:obituary
DESCRIPTION:Larrell Keith "Sam" Newlin\, 82\, of Bucklin\, Missouri\, pass
 ed away at his home on Sunday\, July 19\, 2026. Sam was born on November 9
 \, 1943\, in Macon County\, Missouri\, to William T. and Myrna E. (Swaidne
 r) Newlin. He was a graduate of Bucklin High School. A lifelong cattle far
 mer\, Sam dedicated his life to agriculture and took great pride in caring
  for the land. Sam proudly served his country in the United States Army fr
 om 1968 until 1970 and was stationed at Fort Sill\, Oklahoma. Above all el
 se\, Sam cherished his family. He especially treasured the time he spent w
 ith his grandchildren\, who brought him immense joy. He enjoyed classic ca
 rs\, listening to music\, spending time with friends\, and relaxing outdoo
 rs whenever he could. Sam also had a special love for all animals and foun
 d great happiness in their companionship. He is survived by his son\, Nath
 an Newlin and wife\, Kristi\, of Meadville\, Missouri\; his daughter\, Dev
 in Bussman and husband\, Chris\, of Bucklin\, Missouri\; his grandchildren
 \, Logan Newlin and wife\, Caylie\, of Brookfield\, Ethan Newlin of Marcel
 ine\, Sevilla Bussman of Marceline\, and Addison and Harper Bussman of Buc
 klin\; one great-granddaughter\, Nora Newlin\; his siblings\, Bill Newlin\
 , Nancy Winkler and husband\, John\, and Norman Newlin\; his sister-in-law
 \, Karen Hanson\; along with several nieces\, nephews\, extended family me
 mbers\, and many friends. He was preceded in death by his beloved wife\, M
 ary Newlin\, his parents\, William and Myrna Newlin\; and his grandparents
 \, James and Letha Newlin. Funeral services will be held at 10:00 a.m. on 
 Thursday\, July 23\, 2026\, at Delaney Funeral Home\, with Ben Williams of
 ficiating. Visitation will be held from 5:00 until 7:00 p.m. on Wednesday\
 , July 22\, 2026\, at the funeral home. The family suggests memorial contr
 ibutions be made to the Veterans Administration.\n\nFull obituary and serv
 ice details: https://www.delaneyfuneralhome.com/obituaries/Larrell-Keith-S
 am-Newlin?obId=49051909
LOCATION:Bucklin\, MO
END:VEVENT
